==Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the German and Dutch language setting of the game, the Goblins' name translates to "Kobolds". In the Spanish, Arabic, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Goblins' name translates to "Duendes", "Ghouls", and "Leprechauns" respectively.
**The Goblins, [[Spear Goblins]], [[Goblin Cage]], and [[Goblin Hut]] are the only cards associated with Goblins that are unlocked in [[Arenas|Goblin Stadium]].
*The Goblins are 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]]. 
**In Clash of Clans, they carried a small bag which was designed to steal resources. Despite their origins, the Goblins carry daggers as weapons, rather than bags for loot as they no longer directly steal loot, nor do they prioritise [[Elixir Collector|Elixir Collectors]] over other targets.
**Their [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] grants them a dark red mohawk similar to the Level 6 Goblin in Clash of Clans.
*The Goblins are 1 of 3 troops which can be spawned by a troop (Goblins/[[Goblin Gang]]/[[Goblin Giant/Evolution|Evolved Goblin Giant]]), a [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] ([[Goblin Barrel]]), and a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] ([[Goblin Drill]]). The others are Skeletons and Barbarians.
*The Goblins are one of the first troops to be featured in Clash-A-Rama, alongside the Minions, Barbarians, and Giant.
*The Goblins are one of the first troop [[cards]] to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, [[Knight]], Spear Goblins, [[Bomber]], Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], [[Skeleton Army]], Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Goblins are one of the first troops to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Knight, Skeletons, and Prince.
*The Goblins are one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Bomber, Skeletons, Barbarians, [[Bats]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A., Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Goblins are one of the first cards to be featured in the [[Season Shop]], alongside the Goblin Cage and Goblin Giant.
*Even though the [[Cards|card]] spawns 4 Goblins, the card render displays only 1 Goblin.
*In their description the word “unarmored” may be hinting at a new card. It is also a reference to the Minions and how it has the sentence and the [[Mega Minion]] was eventually released.
*Goblins are similar to Spear Goblins. However, take note they are not ranged and have to run up to a target to melee. Goblins also have significantly more health and damage than Spear Goblins, despite not looking muscular, like the Spear Goblins do.
*The first Trainer the player battles in the Training Camp uses 2 cards, one of them being Goblins, and the other being Skeletons.
*The Goblins are used by more Trainers than any other card, being used by a total of 25 Trainers.
*The Goblins are 1 of 3 troops that have been featured with an [[Buff#Invisibility|Invisibility]] [[buff]], the others being Skeletons and Bats.
*The Goblins are featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Goblins, along with the Archers, Barbarians, [[Elite Barbarians]], and P.E.K.K.A., were featured as a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Monster monster] in [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_%26_Dragons_Wiki Puzzles and Dragons], in a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Dungeon dungeon] called [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Dungeon Clash of Clans Dungeon].
**The Goblins, along with the Barbarians, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, P.E.K.K.A., and the Archer Queen, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess]. Also along with the Golem and the Archer Queen, it was also featured as a character skin for the Pawn in Chess.
**The Goblins, along with the Archers, Barbarians, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Battle Healer]], Witch, Miner, Ice Wizard, and the Archer Queen, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Characters character] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
**The Goblins are featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Pins?file=Clash_Royale_Pin-Goblin.png a pin in Brawl Stars], resembling the Goblin This is Fine [[Emotes|Emote]].
*The Goblins, along with the Archers, Barbarians, [[Ice Spirit]], Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Giant, Wizard, Hog Rider, Witch, Prince, and Night Witch, are featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-theater-stickers/id1353823484 Clash Theater]. Also, along with the Archers, Skeletons, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and [[Princess]], they are also featured in the [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama] sticker pack.
*Before 13/12/2023, when visiting the [[Shop]], an elderly Goblin with white hair, a brown jacket, and glasses appears as the shopkeeper, holding a Fortune [[Chests|Chest]].
**Prior to 12/12/2017, he was holding a Magical Chest; even earlier, prior to 12/6/2017, he was holding a golden chained watch.
**This Goblin is featured in the Clash Royale [https://x.com/ClashRoyale/status/847796023091224576 Back in my Day commercial].
*In [[Pass Royale|Fisherman's Float]], Shipwreck Island, Goblin-gendary Arena, and Island Arena, Goblins can be seen sitting in the audience.
*In [[Touchdown]] [[:Category:Modes|mode]], a Goblin blowing a whistle acts as referee. This Goblin can be defeated before it runs off-screen with fast spells like the [[Arrows]] if the player is quick enough. [[Earthquake]], [[Lightning]], [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], and [[Tornado]] do not work.
*The [[Rocket]]'s Star Level 3 Skin has a Goblin riding on top of it.
*The Goblins are the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Goblins are the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Goblins are the subject of a few Emotes, for a total of 28 Emotes, the highest amount of all cards in the game.
***The Goblin This is Fine Emote is a reference to the [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/this-is-fine This is Fine] meme.
***The Goblin He’ll Be Back Emote is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terminator_(character) Terminator].
***The Goblin Gob-arian Emote is a reference to the Clash Royale [https://youtu.be/eyni9UgGKc4 The Gob-arian commercial].
***The Goblin Robot Dance Emote is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daft_Punk Daft Punk].
***The Goblin Grinch Emote is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grinch Grinch].
***The Third Anniversary Goblin Emote was originally going to be Exclusive. However, it ended up not being Exclusive in the game.
**The Goblins are the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Goblin decoration is identical to its card render.
***The Red vs Blue and Music Makers frames and Goblin Drummer decoration are created by Myoho.
*During the 1st Anniversary Offer, when the free Magical Chest is opened, a right-facing Goblin was there trying to blow out a candle. The candle would appear on a Miner's helmet if the [[Gold]] and [[Gems|Gem]] pack in the middle is purchased, and a left-facing Goblin will appear if the Gold and Super Magical Chest pack on the right is purchased.
*The Goblins were featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Goblins were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/DVY2TndGf4U?si=ptuVz0tHkkkDIvEl Crown Championship Global Series Tournament], by a player called Sergioramos:).
**The Goblins were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/Sa0QOSJ5AVY?si=Hlcj6efCnFhxfDYe Clash Royale League 2024 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
*On 4/10/2022, the Goblins was supposed to receive a unit count increase to 4 (from 3), but it was [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-40-balance-wip pulled back] until the [[Version History#2022 Quarter 3 Update (26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]].
*The initial balance change for Goblins on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/1/2024)|3/1/2024 balance changes]] was a first attack time interval increase to 0.5 seconds (from 0.4 seconds), but it was changed to a deployment time increase to 1.2 seconds (from 1 second) [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-55-balance-wip last minute].

